  "question": {
    "text": "There are two long co-axial solenoids of same length $l$. The inner and outer coils have radii $r_1$ and $r_2$ and number of turns per unit length $n_1$ and $n_2$, respectively. The ratio of mutual inductance to the self-inductance of the inner-coil is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4O5wr",
      "text": "$\\frac{n_1}{n_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1VxiZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{n_2}{n_1} \\cdot \\frac{n_1}{r_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NmICf",
      "text": "$\\frac{n_2}{n_1} \\cdot \\frac{r_2^2}{r_1^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aU09f",
      "text": "$\\frac{n_2}{n_1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The rate of mutual inductance is given by\n$\\mathrm{M}=\\mu_0 \\mathrm{n}_1 \\mathrm{n}_2 \\pi \\mathrm{~m}_1^2$     ....(i)\nThe rate of self inductance is given by\n$\\mathrm{L}=\\mu_0 \\mathrm{n}_1^2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^2$    .....(ii)\nDividing (i) by (ii)\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{\\mathrm{L}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_2}{\\mathrm{n}_1}$",
    "image": null
  },
